<!--
  navigate_igvc_autonav_2026.xml — IGVC 2026 AutoNav COMPETITION Behavior Tree

  *** COMPETITION TREE — DO NOT FIELD-TEST WITH THESE TIMERS ***
  Duplicate of navigate_igvc_autonav_humble.xml (the field-test tree), tuned
  2026-06-01 for the IGVC 2026 AutoNav run. The ONLY differences from the
  field-test tree are the competition-clock-driven values below; the structure,
  plugin set, and orchestration pattern are identical. The field-test tree
  keeps its 120000 ms Timeout / 8 retries for benchtop persistence — this tree
  is the one that goes on the start line.

  Designed for ROS2 Humble + Navfn (GridBased) + MPPI (FollowPath) on the
  AndyMark Raptor tracked diff-drive chassis (0.7366 m gauge, 0.8 m radius).

  COMPETITION TUNING (2026-06-01), reverting field-test overrides + applying
  the verified freeze-fix recovery ladder:
    - Outer Timeout         : 45000 ms (was field-test 120000) — aborts the
                              single NavigateToPose 15 s before the 60 s
                              Hold-up/Blocking DQ so the orchestrator can skip
                              the wedged waypoint.
    - Outer retries         : 4 (was field-test 8) — exactly the 4-child
                              RoundRobin ladder reachable once each; fewer
                              retries = less dead time against the 1 mph
                              minimum-average rule.
    - RateController        : 3.0 Hz (Jetson-live; laptop tree had 1.0) — cuts replan latency so the
                              global path bows around a freshly-seen barrel
                              sooner; planner_server has 5 Hz capacity.
    - RECOVERY-ESCALATION ORDER (gentlest -> blindest, per RoundRobin child idx):
        [0] ClearCostmapAroundRobot reset_distance=1.5  (surgical local clear;
            preserves LETHAL lane cells > 1.5 m so the next replan can't route
            over a white line — II.4 Crossing-an-Internal-Line E-stop)
        [1] Wait wait_duration=3   (clears stale cells: > semantic
            tile_map_decay_time 1.5 s, at/under STVL voxel_decay 3.0 s)
        [2] DriveOnHeading 0.30 m @ 0.15 m/s, time_allowance 8 s  (forward
            crawl FIRST — has an always-on forward collision check vs the
            local costmap (STVL barrels + kiwicampus LETHAL lanes), re-seats
            MPPI past a borderline gap, clears required_movement_radius 0.3)
        [3] BackUp 0.25 m @ 0.10 m/s, time_allowance 5 s  (short blind reverse
            LAST — no rear sensor, so rear costmap reads FREE; only reached on
            the 4th retry as a true last resort; short distance + 5 s cap keeps
            it from burning the 45 s Timeout)
      NO Spin anywhere (rectangular footprint sweep would cross the 3 in line =
      II.4 E-stop).

  SYNTHESIS SOURCES:
    - TnTech IGVC 2026 (LCAS-Lab/TnTechIGVC2026 :: igvc_bt.xml) — base structure
    - Sooner Robotics 2024/2025 (SoonerRobotics/autonav_software_2024/2025) — orchestration pattern
    - Hosei orange_ros2 (KBKN-Autonomous-Robotics-Lab) — costmap-layer SetParameters
    - RoboJackets igvc-software — back_circle pattern (intentionally NOT adopted; MPPI PreferForwardCritic covers it)
    - IGVC 2026 Official Rules (igvc.org/2026rules.pdf, retrieved 2026-05-12)

  DESIGN PHILOSOPHY — "Dumb BT, smart orchestrator":
    - This BT executes ONE NavigateToPose at a time
    - A separate `mission_manager` Python node (to be implemented) owns:
        * waypoint cursor (lat/lon list, popped on 2.0 m proximity)
        * No-Man's-Land state machine (per-waypoint metadata tags)
        * GPS health watchdog (drop-to-dead-reckon at 2 s degraded, full
          forward-bias-only at 30 s lost)
        * SetParameters side-effects (toggle semantic_layer.lane_white,
          inflate goal_checker xy_tolerance, cap MPPI vx_max on ramp)
    - Orchestrator fires fresh NavigateToPose goals at 2 Hz with whatever
      goal is current; THIS BT is dumb — it just plans, follows, recovers.

  IGVC 2026 RULE-DRIVEN CONSTRAINTS encoded here:
    - 60 s Hold-up Traffic / Blocking DQ      -> outer Timeout msec=45000 (15 s margin)
    - 3-inch white-tape lane crossing penalty -> NO Spin (rectangular footprint sweeps
                                                  2.48 m diameter when off-center);
                                                  surgical reset_distance=1.5 preserves
                                                  LETHAL lane cells; forward crawl before
                                                  blind reverse keeps recovery off the line
    - Remote control forbidden                -> NO AssistedTeleop
    - 1 mph minimum average over run          -> Wait capped at 3 s, recovery
                                                  budget 4 retries x ~8 s
    - Random obstacles every run              -> ComputePathToPose (not ComputeRoute);
                                                  campus GeoJSON graph reserved for testing
    - Mandatory payload, e-stop, safety light -> handled at orchestrator level,
                                                  not in this BT

  RECOVERY ORDER (gentlest-to-blindest, RoundRobin child index):
    [0]. ClearCostmapAroundRobot reset_distance=1.5  (zero-motion, surgical
                                        local clear; no DQ risk; preserves
                                        LETHAL lane cells > 1.5 m)
    [1]. Wait wait_duration=3          (exploits kiwicampus semantic_layer
                                        tile_map_decay_time=1.5 + STVL
                                        voxel_decay 3.0 s to clear stale cells)
    [2]. DriveOnHeading 0.30 m @ 0.15  (~2.2 s; forward crawl with always-on
                                        forward collision check; nudges through
                                        borderline passages MPPI rejected;
                                        clears required_movement_radius 0.3)
    [3]. BackUp 0.25 m @ 0.10 m/s      (~2.5 s; short blind reverse, LAST
                                        resort, only reached on the 4th retry;
                                        no rear sensor so rear costmap reads
                                        FREE — kept short + 5 s capped)

  REQUIRES (Phase 5 validation will enforce) — MUST match the COMPETITION yaml:
    - bt_navigator.plugin_lib_names MUST include:
        nav2_back_up_action_bt_node
        nav2_drive_on_heading_bt_node
      (everything else — ComputePathToPose, FollowPath, ClearEntireCostmap,
       ClearCostmapAroundRobot, GoalUpdated — is already registered in
       nav2_params_humble.yaml plugin_lib_names)
    - behavior_server.behavior_plugins MUST include backup, drive_on_heading,
      wait (already present per nav2_params_humble.yaml). Spin is deliberately
      absent — keep it absent in the competition yaml too.
    - Timeout, RecoveryNode, PipelineSequence, RateController, ReactiveFallback,
      RoundRobin are BT.CPP v3 builtins / nav2 control nodes and need no
      action-plugin registration.

  HOW TO USE:
    ros2 launch avros_bringup navigation.launch.py \
      bt_xml:=navigate_igvc_autonav_2026.xml
-->
<root main_tree_to_execute="MainTree">
  <BehaviorTree ID="MainTree">

    <!-- OUTER WATCHDOG: hard-abort the whole navigation action after 45 s.
         IGVC Hold-up Traffic rule fires at 60 s — 15 s margin lets the
         action FAILURE bubble up to the mission_manager, which can either
         skip the current waypoint or signal the operator-held wireless
         e-stop. Without this, a wedged MPPI could burn the full 60 s and
         disqualify the run on a single stuck waypoint. -->
    <Timeout msec="45000">  <!-- COMPETITION value (2026-06-01): hard-abort the single NavigateToPose 15 s before the 60 s IGVC Hold-up/Blocking DQ. The field-test tree uses 120000 (no DQ clock); this is the start-line value. -->

      <!-- OUTER RECOVERY: 4 retries (COMPETITION value, 2026-06-01). Each
           navigation FAILURE ticks exactly ONE RoundRobin child (retry N runs
           child N mod 4), so 4 retries makes the full 4-child recovery ladder
           [ClearAroundRobot, Wait, DriveOnHeading, BackUp] reachable exactly
           once each — including the last-resort blind BackUp on retry 3.
           Worst-case recovery motion ~6.5 s, comfortably under the 45 s
           Timeout and the 60 s DQ. Fewer retries than the field-test 8 = less
           dead time against the 1 mph minimum-average rule. After 4 failures
           the Timeout catches us via the FAILURE return. -->
      <RecoveryNode number_of_retries="4" name="NavigateRecovery">  <!-- COMPETITION value (2026-06-01): full 4-child RoundRobin ladder reachable once each. Field-test tree uses 8. -->

        <!-- MAIN PIPELINE: replan + follow, with per-step recovery. The plan
             step is throttled by a RateController (hz=3.0, see below) so the
             PipelineSequence doesn't re-tick the planner at the full BT rate;
             the orchestrator additionally fires fresh goals at 2 Hz (TnTech
             pattern). FollowPath runs continuously off the latest {path}. -->
        <PipelineSequence name="NavigateWithReplanning">

          <!-- PLAN step. Wrapped in RateController to throttle the planning
               subtree (without it, PipelineSequence re-ticks the planner at the
               full BT rate ~10 Hz, causing path thrashing and wasted CPU).
               COMPETITION value (2026-06-01): hz=3.0 — adopt the Jetson-LIVE
               replan rate (the laptop-committed tree had 1.0). Cuts replan
               latency to ~0.33 s so the global Navfn path bows around a
               freshly-seen barrel sooner. SAFE on budget:
               planner_server expected_planner_frequency is 5.0 (3 Hz < 5 Hz
               capacity) and the Navfn-Dijkstra search runs in planner_server, a
               separate process from the 20 Hz MPPI control loop, so it does not
               steal MPPI cycles. Keep the RateController (don't remove it) to
               prevent path thrashing at the full BT rate.
               Inner RecoveryNode(retries=1) clears the GLOBAL costmap if Navfn
               fails — stale semantic_layer marks from old camera frames are the
               most common failure mode on this stack (kiwicampus tile_map_decay_time=1.5
               + raytrace patch usually resolves them, but a forced clear unblocks
               the planner immediately). -->
          <RateController hz="3.0">
            <RecoveryNode number_of_retries="1" name="ComputePathToPose">
              <ComputePathToPose goal="{goal}"
                                 path="{path}"
                                 planner_id="GridBased"/>
              <ClearEntireCostmap name="ClearGlobalCostmap-Context"
                service_name="global_costmap/clear_entirely_global_costmap"/>
            </RecoveryNode>
          </RateController>

          <!-- FOLLOW step. Inner ClearLocal removed — when MPPI correctly
               refused to cross a lane, the clear wiped the lane from the
               costmap and MPPI then drove through the now-empty area before
               perception could re-mark it. FollowPath failures now bubble
               straight to the outer recovery sub-tree, whose RoundRobin
               ladder includes a 3 s Wait (child[1]) on the second retry to
               let perception/STVL re-fill (lets stale cells decay). -->
          <FollowPath path="{path}"
                      controller_id="FollowPath"
                      goal_checker_id="general_goal_checker"/>

        </PipelineSequence>

        <!-- RECOVERY SUB-TREE: runs ONLY if PipelineSequence returns FAILURE
             after its own inner retries are exhausted (i.e. ClearGlobal +
             replan didn't fix it AND ClearLocal + re-follow didn't fix it).

             ReactiveFallback aborts the recovery the moment the goal
             changes — GoalUpdated returns SUCCESS as soon as the
             orchestrator publishes a new carrot, so an in-flight BackUp
             stops and the next plan-follow cycle starts fresh. -->
        <ReactiveFallback name="RecoveryFallback">
          <GoalUpdated/>

          <!-- RoundRobin per canonical Humble pattern in
               navigate_to_pose_w_replanning_and_recovery.xml. RoundRobin cycles
               through children on successive recovery invocations, escalating
               GENTLEST -> BLINDEST (COMPETITION order, 2026-06-01):
                 child[0] = ClearAroundRobot  (surgical local clear, reset 1.5)
                 child[1] = Wait              (3 s — clears stale semantic/STVL cells)
                 child[2] = DriveOnHeading    (forward crawl 0.30 m — collision-checked)
                 child[3] = BackUp            (blind reverse 0.25 m — LAST resort)
               then wraps. With outer RecoveryNode number_of_retries=4 each rung
               fires exactly once before the goal fails. Forward crawl is moved
               AHEAD of the blind reverse: DriveOnHeading has an always-on
               forward collision check (projects +vx over simulate_ahead_time
               against the local costmap, which carries STVL barrels AND
               kiwicampus LETHAL lanes), so it nudges the well-sensed FRONT and
               never crosses a line behind. BackUp inherits that check but
               forces negative speed; its rear check reads costmap cells where
               this robot has NO rear sensor (read FREE), so it reverses
               effectively blind — hence pushed LAST.

               Unconditional ClearEntireCostmap on the global costmap is
               deliberately NOT used here — wiping the global costmap forces the
               next planner tick to route THROUGH where the persistent painted
               lane was until perception re-marks it. ClearCostmapAroundRobot
               (reset_distance 1.5 m, COMPETITION value) resets only cells near
               the robot, surgically clearing a phantom STVL/lane flicker hugging
               base_link while preserving LETHAL lane cells and real barrels
               beyond 1.5 m (II.4 Crossing-an-Internal-Line E-stop protection).

               Spin still deliberately omitted: rectangular footprint
               (1.0 x 0.74 m) sweeps a 2.48 m diameter circle when off-center,
               exceeding the half-lane width (~1.5 m) and risking IGVC DQ. -->
          <RoundRobin name="LaneAwareRecoveryActions">

            <!-- [0] Surgical local clear. COMPETITION reset_distance=1.5 (was
                 field-test 3.0): clears a phantom STVL/lane flicker hugging the
                 robot while leaving LETHAL lane lines and real barrels beyond
                 1.5 m intact, so the next replan can't route over a now-empty
                 white line (II.4 Crossing-an-Internal-Line E-stop). -->
            <ClearCostmapAroundRobot name="ClearAroundRobot-Recovery"
              service_name="local_costmap/clear_around_local_costmap"
              reset_distance="1.5"
              server_timeout="5000"/>

            <!-- [1] Wait. COMPETITION wait_duration=3 (was 2): a stale cell
                 clears only after going un-reconfirmed for its decay window —
                 semantic tile_map_decay_time 1.5 s / STVL voxel_decay 3.0 s.
                 3 s gives clean margin past semantic decay while staying
                 at/under the STVL window, so the next replan sees a cleaner
                 costmap. Reached at most once per the 4-retry ladder, so +1 s
                 is trivial against the 45 s Timeout / 60 s DQ. -->
            <Wait wait_duration="3" name="WaitForSemanticDecay"/>

            <!-- [2] Forward crawl FIRST (moved ahead of BackUp for competition,
                 2026-06-01). COMPETITION dist 0.30 / speed 0.15 / time 8 (was
                 0.15 / 0.10 / 10). DriveOnHeading's onRun maps target.x->dist,
                 speed, time_allowance (all positive). 0.30 m @ 0.15 m/s is
                 ~2.2 s effective, well under time_allowance 8 s. The
                 unconditional isCollisionFree check (Humble has no disable
                 port) simulates ~2.0 s = 0.30 m of forward lookahead against
                 the local costmap (STVL barrels + LETHAL lanes), aborting
                 before driving into a dead-ahead obstacle or white line. The
                 0.30 m nudge re-seats MPPI past a borderline gap and clears
                 required_movement_radius 0.3 (the old 0.15 m moved base_link
                 only ~half a rear-inscribed-radius and barely re-seeded the
                 planner). Strictly safer than the blind BackUp below. -->
            <DriveOnHeading dist_to_travel="0.30"
                            speed="0.15"
                            time_allowance="8"
                            name="CrawlForward"/>

            <!-- [3] Short blind reverse, LAST resort (only reached on the 4th
                 retry). COMPETITION backup_dist 0.25 / backup_speed 0.10 /
                 time_allowance 5 (was 0.3 / 0.10 / 25). back_up.cpp forces
                 backup_speed negative; the behavior ends on whichever of
                 distance-reached or time_allowance-expired comes first.
                 0.25 m @ 0.10 m/s = 2.5 s nominal; time_allowance 5 gives ~2x
                 headroom (covers the actuator slew ramp without prematurely
                 FAILING the maneuver). The critical fix is 25 -> 5: at 25 s a
                 wedged/under-delivering BackUp could consume over half the 45 s
                 competition Timeout in one cycle. With NO rear sensor the rear
                 costmap reads FREE, so this is effectively blind — kept short,
                 slow, and last in the RoundRobin. Right-sized rectangle
                 footprint (rear edge -0.2794) means it is no longer
                 collision-blocked at cycle zero. -->
            <BackUp backup_dist="0.25"
                    backup_speed="0.10"
                    time_allowance="5"
                    name="ShortBackup"/>

          </RoundRobin>
        </ReactiveFallback>

      </RecoveryNode>
    </Timeout>

  </BehaviorTree>
</root>
